# Root .dockerignore -- belt-and-braces only.
#
# No build workflow uses `context: .`; all six use leaf subdirectories
# (docker/ctfd, docker/orchestrator, operator/analyst, operator/kali-novnc,
# operator/targets/base-linux, operator/tcp-gateway), and each of those has
# its own .dockerignore. This file exists purely for the failure mode those
# per-context files cannot cover: a `context: .` typo in a build workflow
# would otherwise put docker/secrets/ and docker/.env into a context that
# gets pushed to the PUBLIC ghcr.io/stoptalkingishh/* registry.
#
# It is inert today. If a build ever legitimately needs the repository root
# as its context, review this file first -- in particular the docker/
# exclusions below, which would break `COPY docker/...`.

.git/
.github/
.venv/
venv/

# Live secrets and env overrides. The .example files are kept so the stack
# validation job's placeholder setup still works if the root is ever built.
docker/.env
docker/.env.*
!docker/.env.example
docker/secrets/
!docker/secrets.example/
docker/traefik/certs/
docker/traefik/dynamic/

# Python build/test artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Not needed to build any image
docs/
tests/

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
